      "created_at": "2021-03-18T23:07:17Z",
      "updated_at": "2021-03-18T23:07:17Z",
      "body": "this seems closely related to https://github.com/prebid/Prebid.js/issues/6289 . I personally don't get the idea that prebid.js needs consent to write cookies. Publishers can write cookies such as this so that their site works properly, and prebid is a part of their site, deployed by them. This is a part of how prebid functions. I cannot envision a scenario where a regulator objects to this cookie, as publishers using prebid set it to better comply with the law, similar to how a cmp sets values related to consent. \r\n\r\nHowever, if others disagree, I suppose one could check to make sure prebid vendor id has purpose 1 consent, but I think that should not be the default behavior, as prebid in this case is not setting the cookie like it does in the sharedid sennse, the publisher is. \r\n\r\nI think it makes sense to document this at https://docs.prebid.org/dev-docs/modules/userId.html#how-it-works so anyone looking for this string on our documentation finds the explanation easily. This probably should have been done with https://github.com/prebid/Prebid.js/pull/5451",
      "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
      "pin": null,
