      "created_at": "2021-04-07T13:52:13Z",
      "updated_at": "2021-04-07T13:52:58Z",
      "body": "I don't get it,  this cookie literally stores the consent. It is not a third party cookie but it is a first party cookie that enables the publisher to comply with the law, similar to how one might store \"opt out\" as a cookie.  How are opt outs to function if one can't store them?",
      "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
