      "body": "@patmmccann I generally agree with you...but I wonder if we just move the code that reads and writes the consent hash until after the gdpr checks?\r\n\r\nwhat if we move \r\nhttps://github.com/id5io/Prebid.js/blob/master/modules/userId/index.js#L487-L488 \r\n```\r\n    const storedConsentData = getStoredConsentData();\r\n    setStoredConsentData(consentData);\r\n```\r\n\r\nto just after this block (instead of just before it)?\r\nhttps://github.com/id5io/Prebid.js/blob/master/modules/userId/index.js#L490-L495\r\n```\r\n    // gdpr consent with purpose one is required, otherwise exit immediately\r\n    let {userIdModules, hasValidated} = validateGdprEnforcement(submodules, consentData);\r\n    if (!hasValidated && !hasGDPRConsent(consentData)) {\r\n      utils.logWarn(`${MODULE_NAME} - gdpr permission not valid for local storage or cookies, exit module`);\r\n      return;\r\n    }\r\n```",
