      "created_at": "2023-01-24T16:56:27Z",
      "updated_at": "2023-01-24T16:56:27Z",
      "body": "This fix doesn't work, at least in the case where the CMP is loaded after PBJS. \r\n\r\nSee https://www.eniro.se/?pbjs_debug=true -- there are two issues on a page that we'd like to explore. Here's how to reproduce the issue:\r\n\r\n1) either be in the EEA or VPN into the EEA\r\n2) delete your cookies for eniro.se\r\n3) Don't answer the CMP (AVBÖJ is deny consent, GODKÄNN is grant consent)\r\n4) Check your cookies for the domain\r\n\r\n### Issue 1: The _pbjs_userid_consent_data cookie is set\r\nSetting this cookie seems counter to what this this issue was about.\r\n\r\nI believe it's set because userId/index.js calls setStoredConsentData before GDPR check in initSubmodules. A comment there says:\r\n```\r\n// we always want the latest consentData stored, even if we don't execute any submodules\r\n```\r\nBecause consentData is null, the default data stored with the _pbjs_userid_consent_data cookie assumes `gdprApplies: false`\r\n\r\n### Issue 2: The sharedId PublisherCommonId cookie is set\r\n\r\nNot sure exactly how this is supposed to work but a couple of observations:\r\n\r\n- sharedId has VENDORLESS_GVLID\r\n- the hasPurpose1Consent function returns `true` when consentData is null\r\n\r\n\r\n### Debugging tip\r\n\r\nYou can set up Requestly (or another redirection tool) to redirect the load of https://ads.rubiconproject.com/prebid/14110_Eniro_se.js to https://ads.rubiconproject.com/prebid/14110_Eniro_se-unmin.js\r\n\r\nThe Prebid.js portion of the file being unminified helps when you're trying to set a breakpoint.",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "pin": null,
